
Draft 1 - Traditionally drawn, biro pen / Copic marker:
Larger focus on buildup of visual interest and functionality over proportions and design goal. 
I use greebling to seperate segments of the body which would be manufactured seperately and inspire future functionality.
This draft aims to be a 'brainstorm' for what I desire in this mech.
The next draft aims to give structure to these ideas/

Draft 2 - Digitally drawn, Krita:
Greater focus of proportion and design goals over design complexity. 
This draft aims to make refine of the previous iteration's form and key mechanical functions. 
I tried to apply pointed slope shape language across the body (white) for a more harmonious design composition. 
The white helmet and coloured horns are reminiscent of a Gundam whilst the rounded shape and eyes take inspiration from a Ghanaian fertility doll's large head 
(large heads symbollise intelligence in these dolls).
I tried to implement broad block shapes (yellow) in reference to the wooden material which Ghanaian fertility dolls are made of.


